From 8fc12f40e31c334e790116636c785f90f93dbe61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:02:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run on Windows: portable file locks and syncs

solweig_light imports fcntl unconditionally, and also fsyncs directories,
fsyncs read-only handles and marks cache files read-only. None of that works
on Windows, so the package fails there with No module named 'fcntl'.

src/solweig_light/_portable.py keeps the exact POSIX calls and, on Windows,
uses msvcrt byte-range locks, skips directory fsync, fsyncs through a
writable handle and does not mark files read-only. persistence,
cache/geometry, geometry/service, geometry/visibility_native and
wind_resources call it instead. On Linux, TMRT/UTCI are bitwise identical
before and after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019hAbRjTLoRBAdS6dr9Xkwy
